{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-105618" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the quotient of $2{x}^{4}+{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+13x-7$ divided by $2{x}^{2}+3x-4?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075687/state.json" "file_sha256" "950008a4b73c1140cc9d91b827e1b26f3be3f3156027dace6e381be262623fa4"} {"question" "q-105618" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x}^{2}-x+3 \\\\  & 2{x}^{2}+3x-4\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,2{x}^{4}+{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+13x-7\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{2{x}^{4}+3{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+13x-7 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,2{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+4x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6{x}^{2}+9x-7 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6{x}^{2}+9x-12}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n- the quotient is ${x}^{2}-x+3,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075687/state.json" "file_sha256" "950008a4b73c1140cc9d91b827e1b26f3be3f3156027dace6e381be262623fa4"} {"question" "q-105618" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075687/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b7cd7e541db91571e1702984e71a47a645ad112fe3917db8bc9fe4da07a104f9"} {"question" "q-105618" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075687/state.json" "file_sha256" "950008a4b73c1140cc9d91b827e1b26f3be3f3156027dace6e381be262623fa4"} {"question" "q-105618" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{x}^{2}+x+3"] ["math" "2{x}^{2}-x-3"] ["math" "{x}^{2}+x+4"] ["math" "{x}^{2}-x+3"] ["math" "{x}^{2}-x+4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075687/state.json" "file_sha256" "950008a4b73c1140cc9d91b827e1b26f3be3f3156027dace6e381be262623fa4"} {"question" "q-105618" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{2}-x+3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075687/state.json" "file_sha256" "950008a4b73c1140cc9d91b827e1b26f3be3f3156027dace6e381be262623fa4"} {"question" "q-114515" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the quotient of ${x}^{4}-3{x}^{2}-4$ divided by ${x}^{2}+1?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075687/state.json" "file_sha256" "950008a4b73c1140cc9d91b827e1b26f3be3f3156027dace6e381be262623fa4"} {"question" "q-114515" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that the dividend is missing the ${x}^{3}$ and $x$ terms. So, we first rewrite it by including the missing terms with zero coefficients, as follows:\n\n$$\n{x}^{4}-3{x}^{2}-4={x}^{4}+0{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+0x-4\n$$\n\nNow, using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x}^{2}-4 \\\\  & {x}^{2}+1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{4}+0{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+0x-4\\,\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{4}+0{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-4{x}^{2}+0x-4 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,4{x}^{2}+0x-4}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n- the quotient is ${x}^{2}-4,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075687/state.json" "file_sha256" "950008a4b73c1140cc9d91b827e1b26f3be3f3156027dace6e381be262623fa4"} {"question" "q-114515" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075687/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b7cd7e541db91571e1702984e71a47a645ad112fe3917db8bc9fe4da07a104f9"} {"question" "q-114515" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075687/state.json" "file_sha256" "950008a4b73c1140cc9d91b827e1b26f3be3f3156027dace6e381be262623fa4"} {"question" "q-114515" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{x}^{2}+4"] ["math" "{x}^{2}+4x-1"] ["math" "{x}^{2}-4"] ["math" "{x}^{2}-4x+1"] ["math" "{x}^{2}-x-4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075687/state.json" "file_sha256" "950008a4b73c1140cc9d91b827e1b26f3be3f3156027dace6e381be262623fa4"} {"question" "q-114515" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{2}-4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075687/state.json" "file_sha256" "950008a4b73c1140cc9d91b827e1b26f3be3f3156027dace6e381be262623fa4"} {"question" "q-325111" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $\\frac{-6{x}^{4}+25{x}^{3}-28{x}^{2}+x+13}{3{x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}+x+4}$ in the form $q(x)+\\frac{r(x)}{3{x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}+x+4},$ where $q(x)$ is the quotient and $r(x)$ is the remainder of the division.$$\n\n| $-6{x}^{4}+25{x}^{3}-28{x}^{2}+x+13$ | __ | {{field-1}} | $+$ | {{field-2}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $3{x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}+x+4$ | __ |  |  | $3{x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}+x+4$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075687/state.json" "file_sha256" "950008a4b73c1140cc9d91b827e1b26f3be3f3156027dace6e381be262623fa4"} {"question" "q-325111" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-2x+5 \\\\  & 3{x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}+x+4\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,-6{x}^{4}+25{x}^{3}-28{x}^{2}+x+13\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\,-\\,6{x}^{4}+10{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-8x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,15{x}^{3}-26{x}^{2}+9x+13 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{15{x}^{3}-25{x}^{2}+5x+20}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-{x}^{2}+4x-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n- the quotient is $-2x+5,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $-{x}^{2}+4x-7.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{-6{x}^{4}+25{x}^{3}-28{x}^{2}+x+13}{3{x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}+x+4}=-2x+5\\,+\\,\\frac{(-{x}^{2}+4x-7)}{3{x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}+x+4}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075687/state.json" "file_sha256" "950008a4b73c1140cc9d91b827e1b26f3be3f3156027dace6e381be262623fa4"} {"question" "q-325111" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075687/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b7cd7e541db91571e1702984e71a47a645ad112fe3917db8bc9fe4da07a104f9"} {"question" "q-325111" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075687/state.json" "file_sha256" "950008a4b73c1140cc9d91b827e1b26f3be3f3156027dace6e381be262623fa4"} {"question" "q-325111" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2x+5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075687/state.json" "file_sha256" "950008a4b73c1140cc9d91b827e1b26f3be3f3156027dace6e381be262623fa4"} {"question" "q-325111" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075687/state.json" "file_sha256" "950008a4b73c1140cc9d91b827e1b26f3be3f3156027dace6e381be262623fa4"} {"question" "q-325111" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-x^2+4x-7"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075687/state.json" "file_sha256" "950008a4b73c1140cc9d91b827e1b26f3be3f3156027dace6e381be262623fa4"} {"question" "q-325150" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $\\frac{2{x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+1}{\\,{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+x-4\\,}$ in the form $q(x)+\\frac{r(x)}{\\,{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+x-4\\,},$ where $q(x)$ is the quotient and $r(x)$ is the reminder of the division.$$\n\n| $2{x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+1$ | __ | {{field-1}} | $+$ | {{field-2}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+x-4$ | __ |  |  | ${x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+x-4$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075687/state.json" "file_sha256" "950008a4b73c1140cc9d91b827e1b26f3be3f3156027dace6e381be262623fa4"} {"question" "q-325150" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that the dividend is missing the $x$ term. So, we first rewrite it by including the missing term with a zero coefficient, as follows:\n\n$$\n2{x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+1\\,=\\,2{x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+0x+1\n$$\n\nNow, using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2x+1 \\\\  & {x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+x-4\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,2{x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+0x+1\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{2{x}^{4}-4{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-8x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+8x+1 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+x-4}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3{x}^{2}+7x+5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n- the quotient is $2x+1,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $3{x}^{2}+7x+5.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2{x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+1}{\\,{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+x-4\\,} & =2x+1+\\frac{3{x}^{2}+7x+5}{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+x-4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075687/state.json" "file_sha256" "950008a4b73c1140cc9d91b827e1b26f3be3f3156027dace6e381be262623fa4"} {"question" "q-325150" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075687/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b7cd7e541db91571e1702984e71a47a645ad112fe3917db8bc9fe4da07a104f9"} {"question" "q-325150" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075687/state.json" "file_sha256" "950008a4b73c1140cc9d91b827e1b26f3be3f3156027dace6e381be262623fa4"} {"question" "q-325150" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2x+1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075687/state.json" "file_sha256" "950008a4b73c1140cc9d91b827e1b26f3be3f3156027dace6e381be262623fa4"} {"question" "q-325150" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075687/state.json" "file_sha256" "950008a4b73c1140cc9d91b827e1b26f3be3f3156027dace6e381be262623fa4"} {"question" "q-325150" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3x^2+7x+5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075687/state.json" "file_sha256" "950008a4b73c1140cc9d91b827e1b26f3be3f3156027dace6e381be262623fa4"} {"question" "q-325151" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $\\frac{-9{x}^{3}+22x}{\\,-3x+4\\,}$ in the form $q(x)+\\frac{r(x)}{\\,-3x+4\\,},$ where $q(x)$ is the quotient and $r(x)$ is the reminder of the division.$$\n\n| $-9{x}^{3}+22x$ | __ | {{field-1}} | $+$ | {{field-2}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-3x+4$ | __ |  |  | $-3x+4$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075687/state.json" "file_sha256" "950008a4b73c1140cc9d91b827e1b26f3be3f3156027dace6e381be262623fa4"} {"question" "q-325151" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that the dividend is missing the ${x}^{2}$ term and the constant term. So, we first rewrite it by including the missing terms with zero coefficients, as follows:\n\n$$\n-9{x}^{3}+22x\\,=\\,-9{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+22x+0\n$$\n\nNow, using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3{x}^{2}+4x-2 \\\\  & -3x+4\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,-9{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+22x+0\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-9{x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-12{x}^{2}+22x+0 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,12{x}^{2}+16x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6x+0 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\,6x-8}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n- the quotient is $3{x}^{2}+4x-2,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $8.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-9{x}^{3}+22x}{\\,-3x+4\\,} & =3{x}^{2}+4x-2+\\frac{8}{-3x+4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075687/state.json" "file_sha256" "950008a4b73c1140cc9d91b827e1b26f3be3f3156027dace6e381be262623fa4"} {"question" "q-325151" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075687/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b7cd7e541db91571e1702984e71a47a645ad112fe3917db8bc9fe4da07a104f9"} {"question" "q-325151" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075687/state.json" "file_sha256" "950008a4b73c1140cc9d91b827e1b26f3be3f3156027dace6e381be262623fa4"} {"question" "q-325151" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3x^2+4x-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075687/state.json" "file_sha256" "950008a4b73c1140cc9d91b827e1b26f3be3f3156027dace6e381be262623fa4"} {"question" "q-325151" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075687/state.json" "file_sha256" "950008a4b73c1140cc9d91b827e1b26f3be3f3156027dace6e381be262623fa4"} {"question" "q-325151" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075687/state.json" "file_sha256" "950008a4b73c1140cc9d91b827e1b26f3be3f3156027dace6e381be262623fa4"}] "usage" {} "basis" 2764 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
